     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum single dose of 850\u20131000 mg. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO twice daily or three times daily, if you're starting or titrating\n- 1700 mg as the total daily dose, which would be split into something like 850 mg twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily as written, tell me that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
